--------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. WHAT IS ALREADY DONE ON SAMA'S SIDE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  - SQLite database (auto-created on first run, no installation needed)
  - All models (User, Racer, Organizer, Administrator, Race,
    Registration, AccessRequest, License, RaceResult, ResultEntry,
    PaymentProfile, SystemSettings, Review)
  - All enums (CategoryLevel, RaceType, RegistrationStatus,
    RequestStatus, StarRating)
  - All repositories (6 needed + 3 empty stubs)
  - Builder pattern (RaceBuilder)
  - Observer pattern (CategoryUpgradeService + 2 observers)
  - Seed data: Ardass Sardas (admin), Christian Robins (organizer),
    3 races

  Do not edit any file inside:
    src/bikr/model/
    src/bikr/repository/
    src/bikr/pattern/
    src/bikr/config/
    sql/

--------------------------------------------------------------------
  2. REPOSITORY METHODS — FULL REFERENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  All repositories throw RuntimeException on DB failure.
  No need for further error handling


  USER REPOSITORY (UserRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insertRacer(Racer r)
      Inserts into users + racers tables. Returns new user_id.
      Use for racer sign-up.

  int insertOrganizer(Organizer o)
      Inserts into users + organizers tables. Returns new user_id.
      Use for organizer sign-up.

  int insertAdministrator(Administrator a)
      Same idea, for admin. You likely won't need this.

  User findByEmail(String email)
      Returns a Racer, Organizer, or Administrator depending on
      the role column. Returns null if no match. Use for sign-in.

  User findBySsn(String ssn)
      Same but matches on SSN. Use for admin sign-in.

  Racer findRacerById(int userId)
      Returns a fully-loaded Racer (with currentPodiums + category).
      Use in the results + upgrade flow.

  void updateRacerCategory(int userId, CategoryLevel newCategory,
                           int newPodiums)
      Updates the racer's category and podium count. Called by the
      upgrade service — you probably won't call it directly.


  ACCESS REQUEST REPOSITORY (AccessRequestRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insert(AccessRequest ar)
      Creates a new PENDING request for an organizer.

  List<AccessRequest> findPending()
      Returns all requests with status PENDING.
      Use in the admin approval queue.

  void updateStatus(int requestId, RequestStatus status)
      Marks a request as APPROVED or DECLINED.


  RACE REPOSITORY (RaceRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insert(Race race)
      Inserts a race. Use in the (stubbed) create-race path.

  List<Race> findAll()
      Returns every race. Use for the race list menu.

  Race findById(int raceId)
      Single race by id.


  REGISTRATION REPOSITORY (RegistrationRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insert(Registration reg)
      Registers a racer for a race.

  int countByRace(int raceId)
      Counts confirmed registrations. Use to display (x / y)
      and to block full races.

  List<Registration> findByRace(int raceId)
      All registrations for a race. Use when posting results
      (need the racer list).


  RACE RESULT REPOSITORY (RaceResultRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insertResult(RaceResult result)
      Creates the race_results row (one per race/category).
      Call once per posting.

  int insertEntry(ResultEntry entry)
      Creates one result_entries row per racer. Call in a loop.


  LICENSE REPOSITORY (LicenseRepository)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  int insert(License l)
      Creates a license row. Use during racer sign-up.

  License findByUserId(int userId)
      Returns the racer's current license.

  void updateCategory(int userId, CategoryLevel newCat)
      Updates the license category. Called by
      LicenseCategoryObserver — you don't call it directly.


  NOT IMPLEMENTED (leave alone):
    PaymentProfileRepository
    ReviewRepository
    SystemSettingsRepository


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  3. PATTERN CLASSES — HOW TO USE THEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  BUILDER — RaceBuilder
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Chained setters, then build():

      Race race = new RaceBuilder("Cairo Spring Race",
                                  LocalDate.now().plusDays(30))
          .setType(RaceType.ROAD)
          .setOfficiality(true)
          .setMiles(50.0)
          .setRoute("Nile Loop")
          .setLocation("Cairo")
          .setMaxRegistrations(50)
          .setLastDayRegistrations(LocalDate.now().plusDays(15))
          .build();

      race.setOrganizerId(organizerUserId);
      raceRepository.insert(race);


  OBSERVER — CategoryUpgradeService
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Setup ONCE in Main:

      UserRepository userRepo = new UserRepository();
      LicenseRepository licenseRepo = new LicenseRepository();

      CategoryUpgradeService upgradeService =
              new CategoryUpgradeService(userRepo);
      upgradeService.attach(new RacerNotifyObserver());
      upgradeService.attach(new LicenseCategoryObserver(licenseRepo));

  Call AFTER posting results:

      List<ResultEntry> entries = /* entries you just saved */;
      upgradeService.processResult(entries);

  That single call:
    - Reads each racer
    - Increments podium count if podiumCounted
    - If podiums reach 5: promotes them, resets to 0,
      fires BOTH observers

  You do NOT call the observers yourself. The service does.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  4. WIRING MAIN.JAVA
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  Main just wires everything and shows the top-level menu.
  Skeleton:

      package bikr;

      import bikr.pattern.*;
      import bikr.repository.*;
      import bikr.controller.*;
      import bikr.view.*;

      import java.util.Scanner;

      public class Main {
          public static void main(String[] args) {

              // 1. Repositories
              UserRepository userRepo = new UserRepository();
              RaceRepository raceRepo = new RaceRepository();
              RegistrationRepository regRepo = new RegistrationRepository();
              AccessRequestRepository reqRepo = new AccessRequestRepository();
              RaceResultRepository resultRepo = new RaceResultRepository();
              LicenseRepository licenseRepo = new LicenseRepository();

              // 2. Observer wiring (once)
              CategoryUpgradeService upgradeService =
                      new CategoryUpgradeService(userRepo);
              upgradeService.attach(new RacerNotifyObserver());
              upgradeService.attach(new LicenseCategoryObserver(licenseRepo));

              // 3. Controllers
              AuthController auth = new AuthController(userRepo, licenseRepo);
              RaceRegistrationController regCtrl =
                      new RaceRegistrationController(raceRepo, regRepo, userRepo);
              ResultController resultCtrl =
                      new ResultController(raceRepo, regRepo, resultRepo,
                                           userRepo, upgradeService);
              AdminController adminCtrl =
                      new AdminController(reqRepo, userRepo, licenseRepo,
                                          upgradeService);

              // 4. Views (create as needed)
              MainPageView mainView = new MainPageView();

              // 5. Top-level menu loop
              Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
              boolean running = true;
              while (running) {
                  int choice = mainView.showMainMenu(sc);
                  switch (choice) {
                      case 1: auth.racerFlow(sc);         break;
                      case 2: auth.organizerFlow(sc);     break;
                      case 3: adminCtrl.adminFlow(sc);    break;
                      case 0: running = false;            break;
                      default: System.out.println("Invalid choice");
                  }
              }
              System.out.println("Bye!");
          }
      }

  NOTE: Constructor arguments depend on how your controllers are
  structured. If yours already have different signatures, adjust the
  wiring — that's the only part of Main that cares.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  5. SCENARIOS TO IMPLEMENT (the CLI walkthrough)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  SCENARIO 1 — Racer sign-up
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Input: first, last, email, ssn, password

      Racer r = new Racer(first, last, email, ssn, password);
      int id = userRepo.insertRacer(r);
      License lic = new License(id, LocalDate.now().plusYears(1),
                                r.getCategory());
      licenseRepo.insert(lic);


  SCENARIO 2 — Racer sign-in
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Input: email, password

      User u = userRepo.findByEmail(email);
      if (u == null)
          -> "account does not exist, sign up instead"
      else if (!u.getPassword().equals(pw))
          -> "wrong credentials"
      else
          -> welcome + show racer menu


  SCENARIO 3 — Register for a race (with seat count)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Show race list:

      List<Race> races = raceRepo.findAll();
      for (Race r : races) {
          int registered = regRepo.countByRace(r.getRaceId());
          System.out.println(r.getRaceId() + " - " + r.getRaceName()
              + " (" + registered + "/" + r.getRaceMaxRegistrations()
              + ")");
      }

  After the user picks one:

      if (regRepo.countByRace(raceId) >= race.getRaceMaxRegistrations()) {
          System.out.println("can't register a fully registered race");
      } else {
          Registration reg = new Registration(
                  racerId, raceId, racer.getCategory());
          regRepo.insert(reg);
          System.out.println("registered " + race.getRaceName()
                  + " successfully");
      }


  SCENARIO 4 — Organizer sign-up
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Input: same fields as racer

      Organizer o = new Organizer(first, last, email, ssn, password);
      int id = userRepo.insertOrganizer(o);
      reqRepo.insert(new AccessRequest(id));  // defaults to PENDING
      System.out.println("access request to admin has been sent! "
              + "wait for admin approval");


  SCENARIO 5 — Admin approves organizers
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Input: admin SSN

      User u = userRepo.findBySsn(ssn);
      if (u instanceof Administrator) { show admin menu }

  Show pending requests:

      List<AccessRequest> pending = reqRepo.findPending();
      for (AccessRequest ar : pending) {
          User requester = userRepo.findRacerById(ar.getUserId());
          // or look up name another way
          System.out.print("Accept " + requester.getFullName()
                  + ", yes or no? ");
          String answer = sc.next();
          reqRepo.updateStatus(ar.getRequestId(),
              answer.equalsIgnoreCase("yes")
                  ? RequestStatus.APPROVED
                  : RequestStatus.DECLINED);
      }


  SCENARIO 6 — Organizer posts results
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Input: race choice, then a finishing rank per racer

      List<Registration> regs = regRepo.findByRace(raceId);
      RaceResult rr = new RaceResult(raceId, someCategory,
                                     LocalDate.now());
      int resultId = resultRepo.insertResult(rr);

      List<ResultEntry> entries = new ArrayList<>();
      for (Registration reg : regs) {
          Racer r = userRepo.findRacerById(reg.getRacerId());
          System.out.print(r.getFullName() + "'s rank: ");
          int pos = sc.nextInt();

          ResultEntry e = new ResultEntry(resultId, r.getUserId(), pos);
          resultRepo.insertEntry(e);
          entries.add(e);
      }

      // *** FIRE THE OBSERVERS ***
      upgradeService.processResult(entries);
      System.out.println("ranks saved and sent notifications to "
              + "racers successfully!");


  SCENARIO 7 — Category upgrade visible on next login
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Happens automatically. After Scenario 6, a racer with 5 podiums
  is promoted. Next login, the new category is returned by:

      Racer r = (Racer) userRepo.findByEmail(email);
      System.out.println("Category: " + r.getCategory()
              + " | Podiums: " + r.getCurrentPodiums());


  SCENARIO 8 — Top-level menu loop
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Just the main dispatcher:
      1 - Racer
      2 - Organizer
      3 - Admin
      0 - Exit


