--------------------------------------------------------------------
  7. RULES FOR THE MERGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  - NEVER edit anything in:
        src/bikr/model/
        src/bikr/repository/
        src/bikr/pattern/
        src/bikr/config/
        sql/

    Those are frozen. If you need a new method, ask Sama.

  - YOUR files are:
        src/bikr/view/
        src/bikr/controller/
        src/bikr/Main.java

  - COMPILE before pushing. Ctrl+F9 in IntelliJ.
    If it fails, do not push.

  - ONE PR at a time. Small commits, clear messages.
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  8. COMMON ISSUES AND FIXES
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  Symptom:  "no such table: users"
  Fix:      bikr.db corrupted or wrong working directory.
            Delete bikr.db and re-run.
            Set Working directory to $ProjectFileDir$ in Run Configs.

  Symptom:  "ClassNotFoundException: org.sqlite.JDBC"
  Fix:      SQLite jar not added to IntelliJ Libraries.

  Symptom:  "Cannot resolve method insertRacer"
  Fix:      Your controller doesn't have a UserRepository field.
            Check constructor signature in Main.

  Symptom:  Observer doesn't fire
  Fix:      You forgot to call upgradeService.processResult(entries)
            after saving entries.

  Symptom:  Racer doesn't get promoted after 5 podiums
  Fix:      ResultEntry.podiumCounted was false.
            Check that finishing position is 1-3.

====================================================================
  9. MERGE WORKFLOW
====================================================================
  Roger goes to GitHub:

    1. Same repo page
    2. Their branch (e.g. feature/controllers) will show the banner
       -> Compare & pull request
    3. Base: main   <-   Compare: their branch
    4. Title: feat: add views and controllers
    5. Create pull request

  Likely outcome — GitHub will either say:

    "Able to merge"           -> click Merge pull request  [OK]
    "Can't automatically merge" -> there's a conflict.
                                   See STEP 2B below.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 2B — IF THERE IS A CONFLICT
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  This is almost certainly on Main.java if both branches touched it
  (Sama's skeleton still has print "Bikr starting...").

   Roger does this locally:

      git checkout their-branch
      git fetch origin
      git rebase origin/main

  If a conflict on Main.java shows up:

    1. Open the file
    2. Pick which version to keep — since it's just a skeleton
       right now, either version is fine (they will rewrite it
       in Step 4 anyway)
    3. Save the file
    4. Run:

         git add Main.java
         git rebase --continue
         git push --force-with-lease

  Then refresh the GitHub PR page — it will now show
  "Able to merge". Merge it.

  If there is a conflict on anything else, that means someone
  edited a file they should not have. Check with each other before
  resolving.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 3 — NOW MAIN HAS EVERYTHING
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  Both main and both branches contain:

    src/bikr/model/       - all classes + enums (Sama)
    src/bikr/repository/  - all 6 repos (Sama)
    src/bikr/pattern/     - Builder + Observer (Sama)
    src/bikr/config/      - DatabaseConfig (Sama)
    src/bikr/view/        - all views ( Roger)
    src/bikr/controller/  - all controllers ( Roger)
    sql/                  - schema + seed (Sama)
    lib/                  - SQLite jar
    Main.java             - still the skeleton


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 4 —  Roger PULLS MAIN AND FINISHES MAIN.JAVA
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  This is the key step.  Roger needs to work off main (which now
  has everything), NOT their old branch.

   Roger, locally:

      git checkout main
      git pull
      git checkout -b feature/main-walkthrough

  Now they are on a fresh branch that has all of Sama's code
  + all of their own code. They can now:

    1. Open src/bikr/Main.java
    2. Write the CLI walkthrough (use NOTES_PERSON_B.txt section 5
       as reference)
    3. Use their controllers, and call Sama's repositories
       through them
    4. Compile: Ctrl+F9 in IntelliJ
    5. Run and test the walkthrough

  Sample start of what they will write in Main.java:

      package bikr;

      import bikr.pattern.*;
      import bikr.repository.*;
      import bikr.controller.*;
      import bikr.view.*;

      import java.util.Scanner;

      public class Main {
          public static void main(String[] args) {
              UserRepository userRepo = new UserRepository();
              RaceRepository raceRepo = new RaceRepository();
              RegistrationRepository regRepo = new RegistrationRepository();
              AccessRequestRepository reqRepo = new AccessRequestRepository();
              RaceResultRepository resultRepo = new RaceResultRepository();
              LicenseRepository licenseRepo = new LicenseRepository();

              CategoryUpgradeService upgradeService =
                      new CategoryUpgradeService(userRepo);
              upgradeService.attach(new RacerNotifyObserver());
              upgradeService.attach(new LicenseCategoryObserver(licenseRepo));

              // ... controllers, views, menu loop
          }
      }

  Every repository and pattern class they need is already in place.
  They just wire them together.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 5 —  Roger PUSHES AND PRS THE FINAL MAIN.JAVA
--------------------------------------------------------------------

      git add .
      git commit -m "feat(main): implement CLI walkthrough"
      git push -u origin feature/main-walkthrough

  On GitHub: open a PR, base main <- compare feature/main-walkthrough,
  merge.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 6 — tell Sama everything is on the main repo so she can make a pr
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  If  Roger's controllers do not compile because they need a new
  method on a repository:

    NO  - Do not add the method yourself
    YES - Ask Sama, who adds it on their branch, pushes, and
           Roger pulls

  Same in reverse. This is what kaeeps both branches mergeable.
  The whole plan falls apart if either of you starts editing the
  other's directories.

  final step : delete this notes file for the submission
